# GitHub auto-requests a review from the owner when a PR touches a matching
# path. Last match wins, so the catch-all goes first.
#
# The specific entries below are not about ownership — every path is owned by
# the same person. They mark the paths where a wrong change fails silently, so
# the code-owner label shows up on the PR as a signal to slow down.

*                                   @TheVessen

# Grasshopper binds wires by index. A param added or removed on a released
# component rewires saved definitions unless it goes through the
# OBSOLETE + upgrader procedure in STRUCTURE.md.
/Plugin/Selva.GH/Features/          @TheVessen

# Source of truth for both the TS and C# generated types. Editing it without
# running `pnpm generate` leaves the two stacks disagreeing.
/packages/schemas/ui-schema.json    @TheVessen

# Runs with repository write access and, for tags, the Yak publish token.
/.github/workflows/                 @TheVessen
/.github/actions/                   @TheVessen
